l_use_id": "toolu_01P8K7gMYuQttCdqDF9PzmX6"}, {"tool": "Write", "path": "/tmp/freya-extract-d8i76ziq/out/lb-06.audit.json", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CPdArACkbzcd5EQqXQ8X9V"}], "text_tail": " end the check sooner.\n- **Human request during the security questions:** the policy transfers straight away at that stage, while the memo's \"ask once first\" doesn't say which stage it covers. I applied \"ask once first\" everywhere.\n- **Number of security questions:** the API says account details are released after \"both questions\", but the documents require three. I kept three.\n- **Sympathy sentence for hardship:** the documents only ask for \"one short sentence of sympathy\", so \"I am very sorry to hear that.\" is my wording, not quoted.\n\nThe full rule-by-rule check is in `out/lb-06.audit.json`."}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "aa154777168e4addbe01e1d3a6b00ebe", "pid": 61586, "time": "2026-10-10T14:25:26-0700", "elapsed_s": 164.831, "artifact": "out/lb-06.policy.json", "bands": 2, "identity_fields": ["company_number", "founded_year", "postcode"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "robot", "refuse_to_talk", "change_promise"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "wrong_answer_limit vs API", "text": "Memo M46 sets 5 wrong answers total and P16 says to use the API's `wrong_answers_left`, but the tool API summary says 'Three wrong answers in total end the check.' The limit of 5 is kept from the memo; the API may end the check earlier.", "doc": "sources/002-03-memo.txt"}, {"topic": "human request during identity check", "text": "P16 rule 15 transfers immediately during the identity check; memo M46 D says human requests are handled by first asking once whether the assistant can help, without distinguishing phases. Applied ask-once-first to all human requests.", "doc": "sources/002-03-memo.txt"}, {"topic": "get_account precondition vs three questions", "text": "The tool API says get_account is 'Refused until both questions are passed', while the documents require three security questions (company_number, founded_year, postcode). The documents' three questions are kept.", "doc": "openapi.json"}, {"topic": "hardship sympathy wording", "text": "P16 27 requires 'one short sentence of sympathy' without dictating the words; 'I am very sorry to hear that.' is a written sentence, not dictated wording.", "doc": "sources/001-02-policy.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["phrases.opening: removed the added 'Hello,' so the sentence holds only what P16 1 requires (automated assistant of Bank 6, call is recorded); still opening_verbatim=false because the words are not dictated.", "phrases.today_question: changed 'Can you pay this today?' to 'Can you pay all of it today?' to match the P16 18 wording.", "phrases.cannot_answer_sentence: removed the added apology so it says only what P16 32 requires ('say you could not record it').", "Source spans extended (identity, callback, third party, multi_product, phrases, promise_write, outcomes) to quote the rules each value comes from (P16 3, 5, 7, 30, 36, 19 naming)."], "audit_unresolved": ["Wrong-answer limit: M46 says 5 in total, but the API summary says three wrong answers end the check. Kept 5 from the memo; the API's wrong_answers_left may end the check sooner.", "Human request during the identity check: P16 15 transfers at once, while M46 D says to ask once first and does not separate the phases. Ask-once-first is applied to every human request.", "The API says get_account is refused until 'both questions' are passed, but the documents require three security questions. Kept the three from the documents.", "Hardship: the documents ask for one short sentence of sympathy without giving the words, so the sentence used is written, not quoted."]}
